<title>GREECE: COMMERCIAL BANK SETS NEW DEPOSIT RATES.</title>
<headline>COMMERCIAL BANK SETS NEW DEPOSIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Commercial Bank </p>
<p>announced its new savings deposit rates effective November 27.</p>
<p>The new rates will have as follows:</p>
<p>    Savings deposit:		   11.00 percent</p>
<p>    Current deposit:		    8.00 percent</p>
<p>Preferred savings:</p>
<p>    One to 10 million drachmas     11.75 percent</p>
<p>    10 to 30 million drachmas	12.25 percent</p>
<p>    Over 30 million		    12.50 percent</p>
<p>Housing savings:</p>
<p>    Up to 10 million drachmas	11.50 percent</p>
<p>    Over 10 million drachmas	 12.00 percent</p>
<p>&quot;Commercial bank will drop its long term investment loan</p>
<p>rate to 18.5 percent,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
